From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 13:47:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 124/225] arm64: sprd: ums512: enable Mali GPU (panfrost) and
 register-level CPU DVFS

Two core-platform subsystems ported from the 6.16 ums512 fork and
validated on the RG Rotate (UMS512/T618) on 7.1.

GPU (Mali-G52 / panfrost), confirmed on device (panfrost 1.6.0,
mali-g52 id 0x7402, shader_present=0x3):
 - clk: sprd: ums512: add the GPU APB reset map + reset-controller
   registration to ums512_clk_probe (mirrors ums9230-clk.c,
   reset->regmap = data->regmap). The reset reorg eliminated the
   6.16 sprd_reset_deassert PC=0x0 drvdata bug, so nothing to re-fix.
 - pmdomain: sprd: restore ums512 power domains dropped upstream
   (ums512-pm-domains.h + dt-bindings/power/sprd,ums512-power.h +
   pm-domains.c match); driver core is byte-identical to ums9230.
 - drm/panfrost: add the sprd,ums512-mali compatible (reuses the
   upstream default_pm_rt_data).
 - dts: add gpu@60000000 + gpu_opp_table, the pmu power-controller
   (GPU_TOP/MM/PUBCP), and #reset-cells on gpu_clk. Board: enable
   &gpu with mali-supply = <&vddgpu> (kept in the board, not the
   shared dtsi, so the generic ums512-1h10 board still resolves).

CPU DVFS, confirmed on device (policy0=cpu0-5 up to 1.82GHz,
policy6=cpu6-7 up to 2.002GHz, schedutil):
 - Upstream 7.1 ships only the SMCCC sprd-cpufreq-v2, which is a dead
   end here (stock firmware returns NOT_SUPPORTED for every
   SPRD_SIP_SVC_DVFS_*), so carry the register-level engine instead
   (sprd-cpufreqhw + hwdvfs-normal + archdata + common + sysfs-normal,
   ARM_SPRD_CPUFREQ_HW). It builds clean against the 7.1 cpufreq core
   and keeps the topology_cluster_id policy-mask fix.
 - dts: add the cpufreq_clus0/1 + scu/periph/gic OPP-data nodes, the
   topdvfs_controller (dcdc_cpu0/1/mm/modem cells) + cpudvfs_dev
   megablock, and per-CPU cpufreq-data-v1 + capacity props. Board:
   dvfs_dcdc_cpu0/1 supplies + &cpudvfs_dev.
 - Split the cpu-map into two clusters (cpu0-5 / cpu6-7); upstream
   lumped all 8 under one cluster0, which collapsed both DVFS clusters
   into a single cpufreq policy via topology_cluster_id()==0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
